4. THIRD-PARTY DEPENDENCIES
================================================================================

This project depends on third-party open-source software distributed under its
own licenses. The direct dependencies in use (resolved at build time; the
lockfiles are authoritative):

  Next.js, React, Tailwind CSS ............... MIT
  sharp (image resizing, via Next.js) ........ Apache-2.0; its bundled libvips
                                               is LGPL-3.0-or-later
  FastAPI, Pydantic, pydantic-settings ....... MIT
  Uvicorn, Starlette, HTTPX .................. BSD-3-Clause
  psycopg, psycopg-pool ...................... LGPL-3.0-only (see note below)
  pypdfium2 (PDF text extraction) ............ BSD-3-Clause / Apache-2.0
  Scrapy ..................................... BSD-3-Clause
  Twisted, PyYAML, sentry-sdk ................ MIT
  PostgreSQL ................................. PostgreSQL License
  pgvector ................................... PostgreSQL License
  pgembed (local development database only) .. Apache-2.0

NOTE — psycopg and the libvips inside sharp are LGPL-3.0. Both are used as
unmodified libraries, installed from their published packages and loaded at run
time, which the LGPL permits in software under any license. A fork that
modifies either library itself must publish those modifications.

CAUTION — PyMuPDF is AGPL-3.0, and for that reason this project does not use
it. Linking it into a network-served backend can oblige this project to offer
that backend's complete corresponding source under the AGPL. Text extraction
uses pypdfium2 instead, which recovered the same Devanagari on the real corpus.
OCR (Tesseract, Apache-2.0) is planned but not yet used. This trade-off is
recorded in docs/adr/0002-text-layer-before-ocr.md.

Authoritative dependency license information comes from the lockfiles, not from
this list. Regenerate it before any release:

  scripts/check-licenses.sh

